        threads:'The thread to cut is the ISO 261 coarse thread nearest the model\'s; where the part\'s sheet gives a thread (its card\'s sizes) cut that one. The Wempe-Norm screws\' (WN-) own sheets aren\'t in the set: their size is the model\'s, their thread a maker\'s choice. Tap the part each screws into, clear the parts it passes through, as the fits above say.',
        bookTitle:'The Wempe Einheits-Chronometer: a build book',
        bookIntro:'<p>Generated from the working model of Gerhard D. Wempe\'s Einheits-Chronometer, as its works drawings were last revised: every part card\'s lines of its parts list (by drawing number), each line\'s fit as measured on the model, its material and treatment as its own drawing gives them (the title block\'s Werkstoff, the notes\' hardening and tempering, the surface marks; nothing from practice: where a sheet gives none, or the part has no sheet in the set, it says so), how it is made (CNC milled or turned, by hand, or bought in), and the part\'s drawing from the model\'s solids, in millimetres. The works drawings themselves are Johannes Altmeppen\'s photographs (dg-chrono.de), not reproduced here; the transcriptions in the repository give what is read off each. What the model estimates is listed in the Wempe README\'s "Estimated, not from the drawings".</p><p>Two builds are worked out to navigate by (the README\'s "The build"): the 1940s build keeps the drawings\' carbon-steel mainspring, the 1950s build takes a Nivaflex strip; both thin the gold spring at its bend. This book shows the 1950s build. Wind it as both builds are judged: turn the key to the end of each stroke, hold it and let it back; let go outright, the fusee\'s blow dents its click and bends the maintaining ratchet\'s teeth (tools/wempe_letgo_fix.js).</p>',
        devsOrig:'as drawn',devsBuild:'the 1950s build\'s, a deviation from the drawings (the drawn part is beside it on its sheet)',
        testsIntro:'<p>The analysis says the design works; only these say a chronometer made to it does. Each figure is the working model\'s own, for the 1950s build (tools/wempe_bench.js under MC_WREV=build; its tolerances tools/wempe_tolerances.js), or its drawings\'. Where the drawings name a test (05 06_20\'s pull on the fusee arbor), it is theirs.</p>',
        get bookMore(){const G={};for(const l of MAKERS)if(l.part&&l.how)(G[l.how]=G[l.how]||[]).push(l);return`<section class="bk procs"><h2>Materials and how each part is made</h2><p>Each line of the parts list by how it is made, with its material as its drawing gives it. The special ones first: what needs a hand, a special supply or both.</p>${Object.entries(G).sort((a,b)=>(/hand|special/.test(b[0])-/hand|special/.test(a[0]))||a[0].localeCompare(b[0])).map(([k,L])=>`<h3>${k} (${L.length})</h3><table class="mk"><thead><tr><th>Drawing</th><th>Name</th><th>Material</th><th>How</th></tr></thead><tbody>${L.map(l=>`<tr><td>${l.no}</td><td>${l.name}</td><td>${l.mat}</td><td>${l.hown}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`).join('')}</section>`;},
